[{:db/id "q-106072/selection/19518834b4a9e5a6805b91623b182c569ba80d44c2f0e29cff81194ed1214532" :answer/id #uuid "504cdae1-8078-53e3-8c42-8480b7b0e7ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106072/selection/8f414d66b8801a1d80fe7c6436793ed71a8029f5eb24a09c7f95076352a83e28" :answer/id #uuid "3fae0557-7c06-5501-bad6-e90c6ea1dd24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106072/selection/0414dc25cd73f7f638a5795c8b4f7aecd03e217b582b3a1e98708563656c080c" :answer/id #uuid "0b2520a3-f463-5681-90f0-2f2104ddbb97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106072/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "2b021777-de03-5c6a-b397-99df22da23d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106072/selection/1077111d16f4bff3a816072fe09fc5f2bd5ba3572a06f39b1632eb532a44c20d" :answer/id #uuid "41bbb2d4-9959-5a3f-83fc-da1644e18d6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106072/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6054114f-e2e5-5444-bc00-736558a64725" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106072/selection/8f414d66b8801a1d80fe7c6436793ed71a8029f5eb24a09c7f95076352a83e28" :answer-field/choices ["q-106072/selection/19518834b4a9e5a6805b91623b182c569ba80d44c2f0e29cff81194ed1214532" "q-106072/selection/8f414d66b8801a1d80fe7c6436793ed71a8029f5eb24a09c7f95076352a83e28" "q-106072/selection/0414dc25cd73f7f638a5795c8b4f7aecd03e217b582b3a1e98708563656c080c" "q-106072/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-106072/selection/1077111d16f4bff3a816072fe09fc5f2bd5ba3572a06f39b1632eb532a44c20d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106072" :question/id #uuid "787d93a7-5fc8-5bf3-9f23-708cb4e4f81a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106072" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transform the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/2}\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}-y=0\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{1/2}\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}-y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{1/2}\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2} & =y \\\\ \\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y & ={y}^{1/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{2},\\,q(x)=1,\\,n=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{1/2}=1.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}z=1\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,z=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-106072/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc2192f-24a4-5160-844c-4d17096779e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106072"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109018/selection/dc52d973f97a064c5c07994195ea9cbcf78d73020ffb6f122bcf2724c2b2909a" :answer/id #uuid "ef62511a-4f0d-52b9-86b2-a801ef3bd39c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109018/selection/e819017e19dccac106b8bdd7a345917915a57ae6ae3646d73f366105b31b91f7" :answer/id #uuid "57449b9a-4aac-510f-bdf1-15ed4844eee9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109018/selection/d83e36851edc7200e51b52b07858c37196c8af7d82c66e780ce30b6d43edaf8e" :answer/id #uuid "f9bf24f1-5120-59d2-b918-c9a9bb3deacf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109018/selection/0414dc25cd73f7f638a5795c8b4f7aecd03e217b582b3a1e98708563656c080c" :answer/id #uuid "2a0db9e2-263a-5233-a6aa-d5225631746f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109018/selection/6c24ebe4bf973f0938fdfbd36c15af68fcd2bb30b80fbae06180f739fb0d5dce" :answer/id #uuid "2060584b-7030-5f93-bee2-7376c2914474" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109018/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "27cfa124-d0b0-5893-8d89-a55349a6c896" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109018/selection/dc52d973f97a064c5c07994195ea9cbcf78d73020ffb6f122bcf2724c2b2909a" :answer-field/choices ["q-109018/selection/dc52d973f97a064c5c07994195ea9cbcf78d73020ffb6f122bcf2724c2b2909a" "q-109018/selection/e819017e19dccac106b8bdd7a345917915a57ae6ae3646d73f366105b31b91f7" "q-109018/selection/d83e36851edc7200e51b52b07858c37196c8af7d82c66e780ce30b6d43edaf8e" "q-109018/selection/0414dc25cd73f7f638a5795c8b4f7aecd03e217b582b3a1e98708563656c080c" "q-109018/selection/6c24ebe4bf973f0938fdfbd36c15af68fcd2bb30b80fbae06180f739fb0d5dce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109018" :question/id #uuid "0647dc2a-05fe-5a08-9885-3f888f72743b" :question/math-academy-id "q-109018" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{4}y=\\sqrt{y}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{4},\\,q(x)=1,\\,n=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{4}{y}^{1/2}=1.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{4}z=1\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}z=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109018/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc2192f-24a4-5160-844c-4d17096779e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109018"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109022/selection/06f687c9f85190025d3c06c83969555431ddd8876761b1b2b4f5330a017a9aa4" :answer/id #uuid "5a49fedd-ffc5-512b-a805-a87508b534c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109022/selection/07efa0ff5885fb59a7cb0366c3e2a5cfad30a1520a95421db8c53a8b2e583777" :answer/id #uuid "047f16b4-7eaa-5deb-b03e-e7f2bfd251e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109022/selection/8f414d66b8801a1d80fe7c6436793ed71a8029f5eb24a09c7f95076352a83e28" :answer/id #uuid "16832318-4eeb-5919-b0eb-7d0f7bd10403" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109022/selection/333fd72a6be5a10df7c282957f6802022e4e7089a93a3585daee7fa79f626a8d" :answer/id #uuid "de6d00e8-a7fb-5dd9-88c5-e66ada7b017d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109022/selection/453f70bda52a9e0236e3c795c01787f6390fe5f029af46f43f5b5d0cffe87d5e" :answer/id #uuid "c27c3218-958a-567e-bbe0-91ee0724c7fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109022/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "64e28f49-279e-59d6-a4f2-1bc08558956e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109022/selection/06f687c9f85190025d3c06c83969555431ddd8876761b1b2b4f5330a017a9aa4" :answer-field/choices ["q-109022/selection/06f687c9f85190025d3c06c83969555431ddd8876761b1b2b4f5330a017a9aa4" "q-109022/selection/07efa0ff5885fb59a7cb0366c3e2a5cfad30a1520a95421db8c53a8b2e583777" "q-109022/selection/8f414d66b8801a1d80fe7c6436793ed71a8029f5eb24a09c7f95076352a83e28" "q-109022/selection/333fd72a6be5a10df7c282957f6802022e4e7089a93a3585daee7fa79f626a8d" "q-109022/selection/453f70bda52a9e0236e3c795c01787f6390fe5f029af46f43f5b5d0cffe87d5e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109022" :question/id #uuid "c44829d6-0133-55cb-8a5c-a20e996f6c52" :question/math-academy-id "q-109022" :question/problem "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{y}}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{2},\\,q(x)={x}^{3},\\,n=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}={x}^{3}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{3/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}\\,z={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}\\,z=\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109022/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc2192f-24a4-5160-844c-4d17096779e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109022"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109029/selection/0d973b35cad92c1c349ef61ca9cd091fb914ab449b1e7c536c413bcff8348a51" :answer/id #uuid "be25130b-1c34-58ab-b815-bac7386e26a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={(\\frac{x}{C{e}^{x/2}-1})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109029/selection/5f3df305b0785715f710e699bea4a96c482a4ee80193ac84e8a74293fbfbab84" :answer/id #uuid "1146dd13-e9b9-532b-aa90-8e065391ffb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{C{e}^{2x}+x+1}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109029/selection/d2fa9eca0aeafa527cc6d670dad9a7e2cf8c46cfbeff28f83544588b476e57a6" :answer/id #uuid "3994077c-f43e-5d06-9d1e-d2342f644b3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={(C{e}^{x/2}-1)}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109029/selection/89f967cbffa2d698681892d9211b0f7ba3c391bc00abfa63d4f89d40d68e3a9d" :answer/id #uuid "5c51abd1-4bb0-55f3-b5ed-d2efb9956354" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{{e}^{2x}+C}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109029/selection/f80d545e6aa56cd89ae82c8303641530b91f575b02951b3e67afd79bb61cb952" :answer/id #uuid "9829d042-e701-5f50-84b4-bcaa5269b3b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={({e}^{x/2}-2x+C)}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109029/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff790ca9-21da-56ed-8672-32ce810cbd5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109029/selection/d2fa9eca0aeafa527cc6d670dad9a7e2cf8c46cfbeff28f83544588b476e57a6" :answer-field/choices ["q-109029/selection/0d973b35cad92c1c349ef61ca9cd091fb914ab449b1e7c536c413bcff8348a51" "q-109029/selection/5f3df305b0785715f710e699bea4a96c482a4ee80193ac84e8a74293fbfbab84" "q-109029/selection/d2fa9eca0aeafa527cc6d670dad9a7e2cf8c46cfbeff28f83544588b476e57a6" "q-109029/selection/89f967cbffa2d698681892d9211b0f7ba3c391bc00abfa63d4f89d40d68e3a9d" "q-109029/selection/f80d545e6aa56cd89ae82c8303641530b91f575b02951b3e67afd79bb61cb952"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109029" :question/id #uuid "00b0a77d-c476-5309-904d-0aecc5479d50" :question/math-academy-id "q-109029" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y=\\sqrt{y}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-1,\\,q(x)=1,\\,n=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}-{y}^{1/2}=1.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-z=1\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{2}z=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-1/2)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{-x/2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x/2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{2}z) & ={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ {e}^{-x/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{2}z{e}^{-x/2} & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-x/2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-x/2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{e}^{-x/2} & =-{e}^{-x/2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =C{e}^{x/2}-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C={C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{1/2}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{1/2}=C{e}^{x/2}-1\\,⇒\\,y={(C{e}^{x/2}-1)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109029/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17061f4e-da7c-58f9-90b4-47bdc21505da"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109029"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109170/selection/d0a66aaf6b7ebc58f750a14f366b08466ae3eae5c23aa9f1e80440f48c48bc4f" :answer/id #uuid "779d22d4-32ad-50cf-bc93-c67e8e96e9ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={(\\frac{{x}^{5/4}+C}{5{x}^{1/4}})}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109170/selection/e1378d73ba38c505f8327ab7e007a68962869a817355a537df72431d44acc64a" :answer/id #uuid "78fd1a01-9630-5403-abfd-3b00bab29c86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{1/4}+C}{4{x}^{9/4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109170/selection/ab4a0cb0de78493716256e476d6c5f8c89be3e0ee8c09b3722e6615232551cb8" :answer/id #uuid "dc27e877-245e-5e4a-876f-f2076a6d2fef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={(\\frac{C{x}^{1/2}-2}{4{x}^{1/2}})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109170/selection/a8400cb03767ead777a4b048bae1daaeae04e57c2066ff9682ef152aaa22149d" :answer/id #uuid "66be850d-8650-5de7-85a5-9cd4ddb3c8b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}+C}{3{x}^{1/4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109170/selection/d3f7c1e42846917e8035a4c2ed5625be48dd5a2d40ae780d24631b8d6ecdeff5" :answer/id #uuid "046ef0da-6f80-5866-a017-efdfd5af782b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={(\\frac{{x}^{9/4}+C}{9{x}^{1/4}})}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109170/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f64f63e-4fa1-560f-b209-4c5259aa8148" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109170/selection/d3f7c1e42846917e8035a4c2ed5625be48dd5a2d40ae780d24631b8d6ecdeff5" :answer-field/choices ["q-109170/selection/d0a66aaf6b7ebc58f750a14f366b08466ae3eae5c23aa9f1e80440f48c48bc4f" "q-109170/selection/e1378d73ba38c505f8327ab7e007a68962869a817355a537df72431d44acc64a" "q-109170/selection/ab4a0cb0de78493716256e476d6c5f8c89be3e0ee8c09b3722e6615232551cb8" "q-109170/selection/a8400cb03767ead777a4b048bae1daaeae04e57c2066ff9682ef152aaa22149d" "q-109170/selection/d3f7c1e42846917e8035a4c2ed5625be48dd5a2d40ae780d24631b8d6ecdeff5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109170" :question/id #uuid "3f7b3833-fb2f-501a-9c17-6d0b0eb8fbd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-109170" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\nx\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y={x}^{2}{y}^{3/4}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y={x}^{2}{y}^{3/4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{y}{x} & =x{y}^{3/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{-1},\\,q(x)=x,\\,n=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3/4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{-1}{y}^{1/4}=x.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/4}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{-3/4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{-1}z=x\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-1}z=\\frac{x}{4}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is now in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{4x},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{x}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/4x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{(1/4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={x}^{1/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={x}^{1/4}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{1/4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-1}z) & ={x}^{1/4}\\cdot (\\frac{x}{4}) \\\\ {x}^{1/4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/4}z & =\\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{x}^{1/4}) & =\\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{x}^{1/4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{x}^{1/4} & =\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{9/4}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{{x}^{9/4}+C}{9{x}^{1/4}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=9{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{1/4}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/4}=\\frac{{x}^{9/4}+C}{9{x}^{1/4}}\\,⇒\\,y={(\\frac{{x}^{9/4}+C}{9{x}^{1/4}})}^{4}\\,.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-109170/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17061f4e-da7c-58f9-90b4-47bdc21505da"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109170"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
